   "gap": "The source extent is the complete original 1922 estimation, information and sufficiency presentation with all regularity qualifications. Not reconstructed on the route, each owed with exact model, sampling and regularity scope and written proofs: (a) the large-p expansions of pp. 335-337 and the 80 per cent threshold of p. 336 (owned body 589-591 says they are not reconstructed); (b) the Pearson-system regime: regions of validity of the moment method and the efficiency contours on the Pearson diagram, pp. 343-347 (figs. 2-4, ellipses 8x^2+6y^2=1-E); (c) the efficiency of the moment estimates of the form parameters (nu, r) of Type IV/VII and Type II curves from the four-parameter information determinant and its table, pp. 351-355; (d) the curves for which the method of moments is fully efficient (log y a quartic, p. 356) and the near-normal moment efficiency (p. 347); (e) terminus estimation by extreme observations for a general terminal ordinate and the rectangular (Vega digits) example with the mean of the extremes and the ratio 3/n, pp. 347-351 (only the Type III least observation is treated); (f) the Poisson series likelihood (p. 359) and the dilution-method estimate with its variance and table (pp. 363-366); (g) the sampling distribution, i.e. goodness-of-fit calibration, of Fisher's L and of Pearson's chi-square with fitted cell probabilities, pp. 357-358 (owned body 892-895 says it is not answered); (h) whether any statistic gives a faster than root-n rate for Type III location at p = 1 (owned body 798-802: not settled).",
